In VS Code, open:
data → Master_Road_Work_Dataset_15000.xlsx
Say: “This workbook is the original source of the 15,000 road-work records.”

In your MariaDB terminal, run these commands one at a time:
    USE drishti_master_road;
    SHOW TABLES;
Say: “The processed records and analysis results are stored in these database tables.”

Show the imported record count:
   SELECT COUNT(*) AS total_projects
   FROM road_projects;
   It should display 15,000.

Display actual stored records:
    SELECT work_id, state, district,
       actual_expenditure, delay_days, status
    FROM road_projects
    ORDER BY work_id
    LIMIT 10;

Show stored ML results:
   SELECT work_id, anomaly_score, anomaly_detected
   FROM ml_analysis
   LIMIT 10;

Show the physical database storage folder:
    SELECT @@datadir AS database_storage_folder;
Say: “This is the folder where the database server stores its files. We access and manage the records through SQL.”
